timestamp=2026-11-04T09:41:46.952Z level=INFO run=2e1ba946 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python << 'PY'\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\n\ndf = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/synthetic_stroke_data.csv')\n\n# Apply technical noise filtering\nnoise_mask = (\n    (df['age'] > 120) |\n    (df['bmi'] < 10) | (df['bmi'] > 60) |\n    (df['avg_glucose_level'] < 20) | (df['avg_glucose_level'] > 800)\n)\ndf_clean = df[~noise_mask].copy()\n\n# Find 3*IQR outliers for avg_glucose_level\ncol = 'avg_glucose_level'\nQ1 = df_clean[col].quantile(0.25)\nQ3 = df_clean[col].quantile(0.75)\nIQR = Q3 - Q1\nlower = Q1 - 3 * IQR\nupper = Q3 + 3 * IQR\nag_outliers_mask = (df_clean[col] < lower) | (df_clean[col] > upper)\nag_outliers = df_clean[ag_outliers_mask].copy()\n\n# For each outlier: check rule\n# - If 50% or more (pct >= 0.5) of other observations sharing the same values correspond to stroke cases,\n#   they are not considered outliers. (i.e. if condition holds, DO NOT reject as outlier?)\n# - If more than 20% (pct > 0.2) of other observations sharing the same values correspond to stroke cases,\n#   a base-2 logarithmic transformation should be applied and the above check should be performed again.\n# The sentence structure is a bit ambiguous, but let us read carefully:\n# \"For observations in `avg_glucose_level` identified as outliers:\n#   - If 50% or more of other observations sharing the same values correspond to stroke cases, they are not considered outliers.\n#   - If more than 20% of other observations sharing the same values correspond to stroke cases,\n#     a base-2 logarithmic transformation should be applied and the above check should be performed again.\"\n# So for an outlier observation, first check: if >= 50% of others with same value are stroke cases -> not outliers (so this outlier is *kept* / not removed as outlier).\n# Else, check: if > 20% (more than 20%) of others with same value are stroke cases -> apply log2 transform and perform the above check again (the \"above check\" refers to the same set of checks? Or just reevaluate in some way). That’s a bit complex.\n# Also note: these are exceptions/alternative handling for avg_glucose_level outliers specifically. So when deciding final status of each avg_glucose_level outlier from 3*IQR, we must apply this logic.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
