timestamp=2026-11-04T09:50:05.500Z level=INFO run=2e1ba946 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python << 'PY'\n# From the task: \"The critical value for the chi-square distribution should be set to 0.01.\"\n# Also: \"For outlier detection in categorical variables, the age of children should be set to no more than 14.\"\n# \"the age of toddelrs should be set to no more than 3.\"\n# These sound like threshold/parameter values being \"set to ...\" \n# For chi-square critical value at significance level alpha, common values are 0.01, 0.05 etc for alpha. So probably alpha=0.01, hence critical value threshold is chi2.ppf(0.99, df) if using upper tail. That gives threshold ~11.34 for df=3. That’s a reasonable number of multivariate outliers. Let us go with that interpretation.\npass\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
