with work_type 'student'? Or maybe in general status student but age <= 3?\n# Also other unrealistic cases: \"smoker\" or \"formerly smoked\" / person working in children\" - maybe work_type is 'children' (common in this dataset) but also smoking_status is 'smokes' or 'formerly smoked'? That’s unrealistic for very young children. Or any person with work_type 'children' who has smoking_status indicating smoking history? Or perhaps the task just wants us to flag specific strange patterns as written.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
