timestamp=2026-11-04T09:51:57.114Z level=INFO run=2e1ba946 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python << 'PY'\n# Let us look at the exact phrasing again:\n# \"In the final step, you should also check whether there are any values among the categorical variables that are unlikely in reality,\n# such as “smoker” or “formerly smoked” / person working in children. Additionaly you should chceck\n# whether there are any toddlers that are students. If so they should be also considered as outliers.\"\n# The slash and examples are a bit unclear. Maybe: look for \"smoker\" (singular form in text) which might appear as a category value? Or combinations like someone who is \"formerly smoked\" AND also \"working in children\" (work_type children)? That gives the odd2 case above - work_type children with formerly smoked? We saw 15 cases of children with 'smokes', and 1 case of age<=3 with formerly smoked (and also work_type was student in that specific case? Wait look back).\n# For patient 52: age 1.8 (toddler), work_type student, smoking_status formerly smoked - that’s both \"toddler who is student\" AND \"toddler/formerly smoked\" which is also odd.\n# The task says \"such as “smoker” or “formerly smoked” / person working in children\" - could be parsed as: values like \"smoker\" (maybe should be \"smokes\"), or \"formerly smoked\" appearing together with \"person working in children\" (work_type children). That matches combinations. Also separately \"any toddlers that are students\" -> outliers.\n# So categorical outliers include: (1) any observation where age <= 3 (toddler) and work_type == 'student' -> outlier. (2) any observation with combinations like smoking_status in {smoker/smokes, formerly smoked} AND work_type is 'children' (or person is a child in that sense)? That gives unrealistic records like children who smoke/formerly smoked - these should be considered outliers.\n# Also the text says \"smoker\" (without 's') as example - maybe the dataset has that variant? Let us check all unique values.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
