timestamp=2026-11-04T09:52:55.099Z level=INFO run=2e1ba946 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python << 'PY'\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.stats import chi2\n\ndf = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/synthetic_stroke_data.csv')\n\n# Build categorical outliers\ncat_outliers = set()\n\n# (a) toddlers (age <= 3) that are students -> work_type == 'student' and age <= 3\ncat_outliers.update(df[(df['age'] <= 3) & (df['work_type'] == 'student')].index.tolist())\n\n# (b) combinations like smoking status indicating smoking/formerly smoked with person \"working in children\" (work_type children)?\n# Also the task mentions “smoker” or “formerly smoked” / person working in children\n# Also check children age group? For outlier detection in categorical variables, \"the age of children should be set to no more than 14\"\nchildren_age_limit = 14\ncat_outliers.update(df[(df['age'] <= children_age_limit) & (df['work_type'] == 'children') & (df['smoking_status'].isin(['smokes', 'formerly smoked']))].index.tolist())\n# But also maybe regardless of work_type being children, just children by age smoking? We saw those cases too - some had work_type student etc., but age <= 14 and smoking. Also some are work_type children. Both are odd.\n# Add cases where age <= 14 and smoking_status is smokes or formerly smoked (unrealistic for real children)\ncat_outliers.update(df[(df['age'] <= children_age_limit) & (df['smoking_status'].isin(['smokes', 'formerly smoked']))].index.tolist())\n\n# Also \"the age of toddelrs should be set to no more than 3\" (for outlier detection in categorical variables context) - maybe other toddler-specific oddities? Like toddler with smoking status as smokes/formerly smoked\ntoddler_age_limit = 3\ncat_outliers.update(df[(df['age'] <= toddler_age_limit) & (df['smoking_status'].isin(['smokes', 'formerly smoked']))].index.tolist())\n\n# Remove duplicates\ncat_outliers = set(cat_outliers)\nprint('Categorical outliers:', len(cat_outliers))\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
